  "judge_reasoning": "# Evaluation Analysis\n\n## Task Requirement\nThe task asks to identify which character in the Unicode decimal range 8900 to 8920 looks like a snowflake.\n\n## Review of Evidence\n\n**Screenshot 1:** Wolfram Alpha homepage with the query \"unicode 8900 to 8920\" typed into the search input — matches the task's requirement to investigate this specific Unicode range.\n\n**Screenshots 2 & 3:** The query was submitted and Wolfram Alpha returned an \"Input interpretation: Unicode (character set) 8900 to 8920\" with a \"Characters\" pod labeled \"Mathematical Operators\" displaying the glyphs from U+22C4 through U+22D8 (which corresponds exactly to decimal 8900–8920). Among these glyphs, the six-pointed star shape at U+22C6 is visible — the character resembling a snowflake.\n\n**Screenshot 4:** A follow-up query \"character 8902\" was submitted to verify the specific character. The result page confirms:\n- Visual form: an asterisk/six-pointed star glyph (⋆)\n- Name: **star operator**\n- Encodings: Unicode **U+22C6 (decimal: 8902)**\n- Unicode block: Mathematical Operators (8704 through 8959), confirming it falls within the requested range\n\n## Consistency Check\n- The Result Response states the answer is decimal 8902 = U+22C6 STAR OPERATOR (a six-pointed star resembling a snowflake). This is fully consistent with the screenshots.\n- The hex/decimal conversion is correct (0x22C6 = 8902), and the character lies within the 8900–8920 range as required.\n- The verification workflow (range query → character detail page) is complete and coherent across all screenshots.\n- A six-pointed star (⋆) is a reasonable and accurate description of a snowflake-like glyph, and it is indeed the most snowflake-resembling character within that range (the actual SNOWFLAKE ❄ U+2744 lies far outside this range).\n\n## Verdict\nThe agent correctly queried the specified Unicode range, examined the resulting characters, identified the snowflake-like character (star operator, U+22C6 / decimal 8902), and verified it with a detail page. The response matches the screenshot evidence.\n\n**SUCCESS**",
